  "text": "Drawing on data from a nationally representative sample, this study examined the associations of the dietary inflammatory index (DII) and serum vitamin D with frailty among older adults. DII was positively associated with frailty and inversely associated with serum vitamin D. Serum vitamin D also partly mediated the association between DII and frailty, accounting for 10.5% of the total effect. In addition, frailty was more common in men than in women, and among adults aged 60–70 years, a higher DII was associated with a greater likelihood of frailty. To our knowledge, this is the first study to examine the mediating role of serum vitamin D in the association between DII and frailty."
